{
  "case": "errors-at-one-place",
  "description": "Several errors at one place (see main.zhang): their order within the place and their ids, in the list by file and position the API answers and in the id-exact list.",
  "ledger": "zhang-server/tests/golden/budget_contract/errors-at-one-place/main.zhang",
  "now": "2024-01-20T00:00:00Z",
  "known_issues": {
    "errors": "KNOWN-ISSUE: DefineDuplicatedBudget has no metas, so it does not name the budget, unlike every other budget error (zhang-core/src/process/budget.rs:15)",
    "error_list": "pinned, not marked wrong: a transfer's two errors come `from`, then `to` (zhang-core/src/process/budget.rs:38-41), and with both budgets undefined only `from` is reported (the `&&` at :38 stops at the first); a posting's errors at an account of several budgets come in the order of the budgets' names (the BTreeSet of zhang-core/src/ledger.rs:308); at one place a BudgetDoesNotExist (reported during the fold) comes before the BudgetCommodityMismatch errors (reported after it), whatever the order of the postings. Which place the load checks first is not pinned: the unconverted amounts are checked after the fold (report_unconverted_amounts, zhang-core/src/process/budget.rs:121, reporting at :142, called at zhang-core/src/ledger.rs:758), which no client sees, as the API orders errors by place"
  },
